  "claim_audit": {
    "original_statement": "All 11 instruments demonstrate statistically significant baseline learnability.",
    "disposition": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED",
    "justification": "1. For high-learnability assets (ADA, LTC, ETH, BTC), the outperformance of tree ensembles (B3/B4) is statistically significant under block-bootstrapped serial dependence and Holm-Bonferroni correction (p < 0.001, CI > 0). 2. However, for high-noise assets (BNBUSDT, XRPUSDT), the lift over naive chance is modest (+0.0366 to +0.0414) and fold-to-fold variance is substantial, making significance marginal for linear and sub-optimal models. 3. Furthermore, XMRUSDT is severely sample-constrained (30,623 bars across 3 folds), limiting inferential power. 4. Statistical learnability (rejecting H0 in Balanced Accuracy) does NOT establish economic profitability after bid-ask spread, slippage, and taker fees. Therefore, the claim is rigorously classified as PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED."
  }
}